-- title:
--   Riesz representation for the weight-2 Petersson pairing on Γ_H(M)
-- statement:
--   Fix a natural number $M$, assumed nonzero, and a subgroup $H\le(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and let $\Gamma=$ [`CohCarrier.GammaH M H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) be the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ obtained by pushing forward along the inclusion $\Gamma_0(M)\hookrightarrow \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism [`CohCarrier.gamma0Units`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L121) sending $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M)$ to the unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ given by its lower-right entry (with inverse the reduction of its upper-left entry). Let $\ell$ be an arbitrary $\mathbb{C}$-linear functional on the space of weight-$2$ cusp forms for $\Gamma$. The assertion is that there exists a weight-$2$ cusp form $f$ for $\Gamma$ such that for every weight-$2$ cusp form $g$ for $\Gamma$ one has $$i\int_{\mathcal{F}}\ \mathtt{petersson}\ 2\ f\ g\ (\tau)\,=\,\ell(g),$$ where the weight-$2$ Petersson integrand is $\overline{f(\tau)}g(\tau)(\operatorname{Im}\tau)^{2}$ and the domain of integration is $\mathcal{F}=$ [`FLT.Gamma0FundamentalSet.gammaFundamentalSet`](def/AutomorphicForm_Gamma0FundamentalSet.html#L13) of the subgroup $\Gamma\sqcup\langle -1\rangle$ generated by $\Gamma$ together with $-I$, namely the union over cosets $q$ in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})/(\Gamma\cdot\{\pm I\})$ of the translates $(\mathrm{Quotient.out}\,q)^{-1}\cdot\mathcal{D}$ of the standard fundamental domain $\mathcal{D}$ for the modular group. Only existence of $f$ is asserted; no uniqueness, and no conjugate-linearity of $f\mapsto i\langle f,\cdot\rangle$, is part of the conclusion.
--
--   This is the Riesz representation statement for the Petersson inner product on the finite-dimensional space $S_2(\Gamma_H(M))$: the pairing $g\mapsto i\langle f,g\rangle$ exhausts the full dual space as $f$ ranges over cusp forms. Finite-dimensionality enters through [`CuspForm.finiteDimensional_of_isArithmetic`](thm.html#CuspForm.finiteDimensional_of_isArithmetic), and the result is used in the construction of period lattices and the Abel–Jacobi map attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$, where linear functionals on weight-$2$ cusp forms must be realised as integration against a cusp form.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_exists_cuspForm_petersson_eq_gammaH.lean

